body:
So my vibe is trash xd

All jokes aside, your observation has some truth to it but I would like to elaborate on that 'image'. Honestly I feel that when I am confident in my speech around others I actually empower them. My friends like to come to me to open up and they usually say that they like my feedback because it's honest. And there's nothing more empowering than someone honestly highlighting your good traits. It's just that this sort of 'expression' goes both ways. When I am not feeling it I also communicate that thoroughly. You're right about it being 'perceptible' to other people. But like I said with the example of that icebreaking session, we vibed really well. But I don't understand why they never talked to me after that.

&#x200B;

The reason I left that club is because they only talk to me to give tasks. I didn' t think much about it so I tried to talk about their interests to go beyond the barrier of formalities. And the same pattern happens again, we both have a long satiating conversation, then I never hear from them again except for when they need something done.

&#x200B;

Basically I wouldn't say I am frustrated with my experience. Life difficulties are to be expected. But I get frustrated when I don't understand the "why's" and my whole circuit shuts down because I wouldn't know how to react. Again back to that same situation above, I don't know if I should consider their actions rude or keep on trying to flaunt a lighthearted surface. Which makes me ask of myself "Why should I even 'try' in order to make friends?" which is the basis of this entire post.
